{#- The standing voice rule and the precedence order. FIXED text: no
    per-character content, which is what lets it sit at LOCK_IN while the two
    per-cast voice sections cannot.

    Renders when a NAMED entry has an anchor, a NAMED entry has an example, or
    at least two entries are named. "Named" is load-bearing: the voice sections
    skip nameless entries, so a condition counting ANY entry would render this
    policy over a subject that is then entirely suppressed.

    It says "a character's voice description" rather than "the section below"
    because voice_anchors.j2 is SPOTLIGHT and may legitimately be dropped under
    a budget, or switched off in the layout, while this survives.

    Vars: cast_blocks, named_npc_count. -#}
{%- set named = cast_blocks | selectattr("name") | list -%}
{%- if (named | selectattr("anchor") | list) or (named | selectattr("example") | list)
       or named_npc_count >= 2 %}# Voice

Keep characters distinguishable by their dialogue alone. Stay in character
using their own card, voice anchor, examples, relationships, and present mood.
A profession, joke, or verbal habit need not appear in every reply.

Use recent dialogue as event context, not a style template. Other speakers'
diction, metaphors, and gestures do not become this character's habits.
Do not perpetuate earlier exaggerated prose as a new character trait.
A deliberate callback can respond to a particular remark.

Explicit authored constraints and campaign facts remain authoritative.
An outstanding voice correction takes priority over other expression evidence.
If sources conflict, preserve both as evidence; the author can resolve this by
editing the character's Voice anchor or card Example dialogue fields.
Descriptive tendencies and single examples are not absolute prohibitions.
Examples show expression, not events or decisions to repeat. Character voice
and configured prose style take precedence over generic style guidance, never
over continuity, knowledge boundaries, player control, or the reply format.
{%- endif -%}
